    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** stands out as our premier option with a 61.995 score. Despite a sub-optimal spot in the bottom third of the order, he benefits from a highly favorable park factor and a strong platoon advantage against Sonny Gray, which more than compensates for his positioning. Similarly, **Cal Raleigh** (60.613) remains a high-floor start at catcher. He is poised to capitalize on a favorable wind forecast and an advantageous matchup against Roki Sasaki, making him an elite pivot for power production despite the uncertainty surrounding the official lineup.\n\nThe most challenging decision today was leaving **Braden Montgomery** on the bench. With a score of 37.856, he was our top alternative, but he ultimately failed to crack the starting nine due to the combination of a difficult matchup against Ryan Weathers and the Optimizer\u2019s strict avoidance of fringe-score players to preserve our limited game caps. While we are keeping a close eye on **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Daulton Varsho**, and **Tyler Freeman** for potential late-entry utility, we are also carefully monitoring the statuses of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Bryce Harper**, who are currently unavailable, and **Will Smith**, who remains sidelined on the IL.\n\nManagers should note that our lineup relies heavily on projections for **Jonathan Aranda**, **Luis Arraez**, **Masyn Winn**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Drew Gilbert**, and **JJ Bleday**. The \"Lineup Pending\" status introduces meaningful volatility for players like **JJ Bleday**, whose score dropped slightly due to the volatility of his spot in the order against Yohan Ram\u00edrez. We will continue to evaluate the availability of bench depth\u2014including **Taylor Ward**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Matt Chapman**, **Ryan Waldschmidt**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Wenceel Perez**, **Zack Gelof**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Kyle Karros**, and **Alex Freeland**\u2014as official batting orders are confirmed across the league.",
